    "q-171618": {
      "dom_id": "step-q171618",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "The solution to the inequality $24<6y$ is $y${{field-1}}{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The variable $y$ is being *multiplied* by $6.$ To isolate $y,$ we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $6.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24 & <6y \\\\ \\frac{24}{6} & <\\frac{6y}{6} \\\\ 4 & <\\frac{6y}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can cancel the common factor $6$ from the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & <\\frac{6y}{6} \\\\ 4 & <\\frac{\\cancel{6}y}{\\cancel{6}} \\\\ 4 & <y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the inequality with the variable on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\ny>4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y>4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
